# Lab 22-1 STARTER: write the acceptance tests for the pump dry-run trip.
# Module 22 (Software engineering).
#
# In this lab the program is finished and correct: labs/22-1-dry-run-trip.st.
# YOUR job is to write the tests. Copy this file to my-work/ and add
# scenarios until your test file
#   1. PASSES the correct implementation   labs/22-1-dry-run-trip.st
#   2. FAILS every mutant                  labs/mutants/22-1-mutant-*.st
# The README explains how to run both checks.
#
# Rules (the same ones the course's own tests follow):
#   - use only the interface variables: StartPB, StopPB_NC, FlowSw, ResetPB,
#     PumpRun, DryRunAlarm
#   - every scenario starts from a fresh PLC, where all inputs are FALSE:
#     set StopPB_NC TRUE first (a healthy NC stop button)
#   - check timing with 'wait' and 'until ... within', never by counting scans
#
# The example scenario below passes the correct program, but it kills no
# mutant: every mutant starts and seals in correctly. Keep it, and add one
# scenario per requirement R1-R7 in the README.

scenario R1 start runs the pump and it seals in
set StopPB_NC TRUE
set FlowSw TRUE
set StartPB TRUE
scan
expect PumpRun TRUE
set StartPB FALSE
wait 1s
expect PumpRun TRUE
expect DryRunAlarm FALSE

